course: dictionary
lesson: 14586
title: Pleasantly, in a nice way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pleasantly is an adverb. It tells you how something is done or how something feels, and it means in a nice, enjoyable or friendly way. «The lady smiled pleasantly at the new children.» Smiling pleasantly means smiling in a friendly way, so the children feel welcome.
explain: Pleasantly can also mean to a nice degree, which means comfortable but not extreme. «The bath water was pleasantly warm.» It was not hot and not cold. It was just comfortable. Ask yourself: is this nice and comfortable, or nice in a friendly way? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: You will often see pleasantly in the phrase «pleasantly surprised». It is a modest, quiet way of saying that something was better than you expected. «Ben was pleasantly surprised by the film.» He did not expect much, but he liked it more than he thought he would.
fact: Pleasantly is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens or how something is.
fact: «Pleasantly» means in a nice, enjoyable or friendly way.
fact: «Pleasantly warm» means warm in a comfortable way, not too hot.
fact: «Pleasantly surprised» means you liked something more than you expected.
fact: Other phrases to know are «smile pleasantly» and «pleasantly cool».
exercise: «The old man smiled pleasantly at the children.» How did the old man smile? | Without stopping | Angrily and with a frown | *In a friendly way | Very loudly
exercise: «The soup was pleasantly warm, not too hot to eat.» What does pleasantly mean here? | Very quickly | Burning hot | *In a comfortable way | Cold and wet
exercise: «Mia was pleasantly surprised by the school trip.» What does pleasantly surprised mean? | *She liked the trip more than she expected | She forgot about the trip | She was very angry about the trip | She was scared of the trip
test: «The breeze was pleasantly cool on the hot afternoon.» Which word tells you the breeze was nice and comfortable? | Breeze | *Pleasantly | Hot | Afternoon
test: Nina thought the play would be dull, but she was pleasantly surprised. What does this tell you? | She thought the play was too long | She fell asleep during the play | *She enjoyed the play more than she thought she would | She did not go to the play
exam: «The teacher greeted us pleasantly at the door.» Which choice is closest in meaning to pleasantly here? | *In a friendly way | Rudely | Sadly | Quietly and slowly
